 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Example\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates how to delineate valley floors using `valley-floor`.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Entry points\n",
    "\n",
    "The package provides two entry points:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `delineate_from_dem_and_flowlines` — the full pipeline. Takes a DEM and flowlines and handles all intermediate steps internally using [streamkit](https://github.com/avkoehl/streamkit). This is the recommended starting point for most users.\n",
    "- `delineate` — the core algorithm only. Takes precomputed HAND, subbasins, and cross section points. Use this if you want to bring your own inputs computed from a different tool or workflow. See the [API reference](../reference/index.qmd) for details.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook uses `delineate_from_dem_and_flowlines`. Both the sample data and this entry point require the `streamkit` optional dependency:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "pip install \"valley-floor[streamkit] @ git+https://github.com/avkoehl/valley-floor.git\"\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load sample data\n",
    "\n",
    "The sample data is a DEM and flowlines for a small watershed in California (HUC 1805000203). Data is downloaded on first use and cached locally."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "OMP: Info #276: omp_set_nested routine deprecated, please use omp_set_max_active_levels instead.\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Loading sample data from cache at /Users/arthurkoehl/Library/Caches/valley_floor...\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from valley_floor import (\n",
    "    Parameters,\n",
    "    PreprocessingParameters,\n",
    "    PostprocessingParameters,\n",
    "    delineate_from_dem_and_flowlines,\n",
    ")\n",
    "from valley_floor.data import load_sample_data\n",
    "\n",
    "dem, flowlines = load_sample_data()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x600 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "dem.plot(ax=ax, cmap='terrain', add_colorbar=True)\n",
    "flowlines.plot(ax=ax, color='steelblue', linewidth=0.5)\n",
    "ax.set_title('DEM and Flowlines')\n",
    "ax.set_axis_off()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Run delineation\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the full pipeline with default parameters. Passing `PostprocessingParameters` applies postprocessing (close holes, remove high slope areas) to the output.
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "result = delineate_from_dem_and_flowlines(\n",
    "    dem,\n",
    "    flowlines,\n",
    "    params=Parameters(),\n",
    "    preprocessing_params=PreprocessingParameters(),\n",
    "    postprocessing_params=PostprocessingParameters(),\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Visualize results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x600 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "valley_floor = result['valley_floor']\n",
    "floor_masked = valley_floor.where(valley_floor == 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "dem.plot(ax=ax, cmap='terrain', add_colorbar=True, alpha=0.8)\n",
    "floor_masked.plot(ax=ax, cmap='Reds', add_colorbar=False, alpha=0.6)\n",
    "ax.set_title('Valley Floor')\n",
    "ax.set_axis_off()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1400x600 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "region_floor = result['region_floor']\n",
    "flood_floor = result['flood_floor']\n",
    "\n",
    "region_masked = region_floor.where(region_floor == 1)\n",
    "flood_masked = flood_floor.where(flood_floor == 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "dem.plot(ax=axes[0], cmap='terrain', add_colorbar=False, alpha=0.8)\n",
    "region_masked.plot(ax=axes[0], cmap='Greens', add_colorbar=False, alpha=0.6)\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Region Growing Component')\n",
    "axes[0].set_axis_off()\n",
    "\n",
    "dem.plot(ax=axes[1], cmap='terrain', add_colorbar=False, alpha=0.8)\n",
    "flood_masked.plot(ax=axes[1], cmap='Oranges', add_colorbar=False, alpha=0.6)\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Reach Flooding Component')\n",
    "axes[1].set_axis_off()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
 ],
